===Etymology 1===
Shortening of {{m|en|application}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|computing|mobile phones}} An [[application]] (program), especially a small one designed for a mobile device.
#* {{quote-journal|lang=en|journal=Maximum PC|date=February|month=February|volume=4|number=2|passage=A visual tool can be thought of as a graphics '''app''' that generates most of your program's GUI code for you}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=JavaScript application cookbook|page=xi|author=Jerry Bradenbaugh|year=1999|passage=So is a spreadsheet '''app''', but I'm not going to put those on a web site any time soon.}}
#* {{quote-journal|lang=en|journal=AUUGN|year=1999|month=November|page=9|volume=20|number=4|passage=The Web browser was the killer '''app''' that kickstarted the Internet and, in turn, enabled it to be embedded in everything}}
#* {{quote-journal|lang=en|journal=Popular Science|year=2005|month=May|page=78|volume=266|number=5|passage=Want realtime flight and gate updates? A calorie counter? A remote for your DVD player? Chances are there's an '''app''' for it. Smartphones separate themselves in another key area: connectivity}}
# {{lb|en|military}} [[application]] {{gloss|use, purpose; not a computer program}}
#* '''1995''', ''The X-Files'' (TV series), ''Nisei'' (episode)
#*: SCULLY: What are these chips used for?<br>PENDRELL: Video games, brake systems, they're finding new '''apps''' every day. I just read about one being designed to help the severely disabled operate computers using brainwaves.

